      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"avant-garde\" or \"experimental\" sounds like a polite way of saying they're testing it on us. it's not just speculation if i'm actually feeling the physical effects in my apartment every night. if this is being used to manage resident \"compliance\" or even just to keep everyone in a predictable state of mind, how would someone even protect themselves? i want to stop feeling this constant, forced agitation. are there any specific ways to shield a room from sub-audible frequencies or disrupt these kinds of electronic modulations? like, what kind of materials or setups actually work against subsonic waves?",
